// Lantern Crossing: a cartographer and a ferryman cross a foggy river before dawn.
//
// Speakers are cast ids from cast.yaml, so a name plate follows the player's language. Every line and option has a #line: id, which strings/zh-Hans.yaml translates and save slots point at. <<bg name>> changes the background (stage.go draws each one) and <<ending name>> names the ending the story reached.
title: Start
chapter: dock
---
<<declare $trust = 0>>
<<bg dock>>
The last ferry leaves the east dock at midnight. #line:dock_01
tobin: You're late. The fog is already on the water. #expr:stern #line:dock_02
mira: I have a map that has to reach the harbor before dawn. #expr:worry #line:dock_03
tobin: Maps don't row boats. What's on it? #line:dock_04
-> Show him the map #line:dock_c1
    <<set $trust += 1>>
    mira: A new channel through the marsh. I charted it myself. #expr:smile #line:dock_05
    tobin: Then hold the lantern up while I row. #expr:smile #line:dock_06
-> Keep it rolled up #line:dock_c2
    mira: Something the harbor master paid for. That's all you need to know. #line:dock_07
    tobin: Suit yourself. The fog doesn't care about secrets. #expr:stern #line:dock_08
<<jump River>>
===
title: River
chapter: river
---
<<bg river>>
The dock lights shrink behind them until only the lantern is left. #line:river_01
tobin: Hear that? Something is knocking against the hull. #expr:worry #line:river_02
-> Lean out with the lantern #line:river_c1
    <<set $trust += 1>>
    mira: A drifting crate, with a name painted on it. Yours. #expr:worry #line:river_03
    tobin: My brother's. He took this route last spring and never came back. #expr:worry #line:river_04
    mira: Then we finish his crossing for him. #expr:smile #line:river_05
-> Tell him to row faster #line:river_c2
    tobin: Faster is how boats end up on the rocks. #expr:stern #line:river_06
    mira: Then slower, but don't stop. #line:river_07
<<jump Fork>>
===
title: Fork
chapter: fork
---
<<bg fork>>
Where the river splits, a light blinks on the left bank and the marsh opens on the right. #line:fork_01
tobin: Everyone follows that light. It's the safe way, they say. #line:fork_02
<<if $trust >= 2>>
    tobin: But it's your map. If you say the marsh channel is real, I'll believe you. #expr:smile #line:fork_03
<<else>>
    tobin: And I don't steer into a marsh on a stranger's word. #expr:stern #line:fork_04
<<endif>>
-> Follow the light #line:fork_c1
    <<jump Lost>>
-> Take the marsh channel #line:fork_c2
    <<if $trust >= 2>>
        <<jump Dawn>>
    <<else>>
        tobin: No. We stay with the light. #expr:stern #line:fork_05
        <<jump Lost>>
    <<endif>>
===
title: Lost
chapter: fog
---
<<bg fog>>
The light drifts ahead of them, then it is gone, and the fog closes in. #line:lost_01
tobin: That was never a lighthouse. It was what my brother followed. #expr:worry #line:lost_02
mira: Then the map stays dry in my bag, and the harbor waits for nothing. #expr:worry #line:lost_03
<<hide>>
<<ending lost>>
===
title: Dawn
chapter: harbor
---
<<bg harbor>>
The marsh channel runs straight and quiet, exactly where the map says it does. #line:dawn_01
tobin: Harbor bells. We made it before the tide turned. #expr:smile #line:dawn_02
mira: We made it. Your brother's crossing too. #expr:smile #line:dawn_03
<<hide>>
<<ending dawn>>
===
